.TH XCLIPY 1 2026-10-29 Xclipy "Xclipy manual"
.SH NAME
xclipy \- clipboard history and emoji picker
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBxclipy\fP [\fB\-\-background\fP | \fB\-\-show\fP | \fB\-\-emoji\fP | \fB\-\-settings\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
\fBxclipy\fP keeps what you copy and opens it in an overlay under the text
cursor, or in the bottom right corner of the screen when there is none. Choosing
an item pastes it into the application you were typing in. The overlay also has
an Emojis tab.
.LP
It runs from login without a window, and its keyboard shortcuts (Super+V and
Super+.) open the overlay. They are the desktop's own custom shortcuts in
Cinnamon, MATE and Xfce, added the first time Xclipy runs there.
.LP
Without an option, \fBxclipy\fP opens the overlay, like \fB\-\-show\fP.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without opening the overlay (as at login).
.TP
.B \-\-show
Open the overlay on the Clipboard tab, or close it if it is open there.
.TP
.B \-\-emoji
Open the overlay on the Emojis tab, or close it if it is open there.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the settings. In Cinnamon, they are also in System Settings, Clipboard.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/xclipy/history.json
The history, pinned items included. Passwords are not in it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/xclipy/images/
The copied images, when the settings keep them.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcinnamon-settings\fP(1)
